[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5799557777","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123766#issuecomment-5799557777","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123766","id":5799557777,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWa46kQ","user":{"login":"MrcotinSol","id":181864359,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtcHpw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181864359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrcotinSol","html_url":"https://github.com/MrcotinSol","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrcotinSol/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrcotinSol/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrcotinSol/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrcotinSol/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrcotinSol/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrcotinSol/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrcotinSol/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrcotinSol/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrcotinSol/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-23T17:25:08Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T17:25:25Z","body":"DISCLAIMER : this issue is not a duplicate of #109940, the origin of the error is diffrent","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5799557777/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5800682936","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123766#issuecomment-5800682936","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123766","id":5800682936,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWb9luA","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-23T18:36:15Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:36:15Z","body":"The analyzer is structured into a \"resolve interface\" and a \"resolve body\" phase. All things that could influence type inference of class members is analyzed in the interface stage, this includes default parameters.\n\nIn order for lambdas to be able to correctly access class members, resolving lambda bodies is pushed back into the body phase. This is done using a list. At the end of the body phase we check whether we handled everything from the list, if we didn't there might be a bug.\n\nThe issue is that this checks happens before we resolve inner classes, so they don't get the opportunity to gracefully handle their lambda bodies.\n\nThe simple and least invasive fix here would be to move the check till after inner classes were resolved. In theory the error print shouldn't cause any real issues because we fall back to analyzing the lambda body, which is the same thing the graceful path would do.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5800682936/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6083211491","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123766#issuecomment-6083211491","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123766","id":6083211491,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABapZw4w","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-09T14:44:24Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T14:49:55Z","body":"I don't think this is the correct fix. The point of the check wasn't so much to verify whether pending lambda bodies were resolved or not, but rather to check if they were resolved _at the right time_. The issue is that the parser and analyzer don't track context very reliably in certain cases. For instance, `GDScriptAnalyzer::resolve_class_body()` assigns the current class to `parser->current_class` near the beginning and restores the previous class near the end of `GDScriptAnalyzer::resolve_class_body()`. Resolving pending lambda bodies at the wrong time can result in `parser->current_class` holding the incorrect class when the lambda body is being resolved.\n\nThe root of the problem lies not with inner classes, but with the fact that a function parameter initializer (resolving during the \"interface\" phase) can contain lambdas (whose bodies must be resolved into the \"body\" phase), i.e. a scenario the current implementation doesn't account for. A better solution would be to resolve pending lambda bodies before the current class changes or, alternatively, to refactor how the analyzer tracks context (avoiding relying on class state and instead either passing needed references through parameters or getting them from AST).\n\nThe least invasive fix (though likely still not entirely correct) is simply to remove the `ERR_PRINT()` but keep `resolve_pending_lambda_bodies()` where it currently is. Do **not** move it to `GDScriptAnalyzer::resolve_body()`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6083211491/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6096502108","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123766#issuecomment-6096502108","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123766","id":6096502108,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABa2E9XA","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-10T10:19:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T10:19:39Z","body":"Thanks for the  insight! I guess that makes sense, but in that case we definitely shouldn't apply a stop gap solution at all I'd say.\n\nI guess this should be sufficiently solvable by using a dedicated queue per function, although we might as well reiterate the initializers in that case.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6096502108/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6096655376","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123766#issuecomment-6096655376","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123766","id":6096655376,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABa2OUEA","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-10T10:40:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T10:40:32Z","body":"Lambda function bodies must not be resolved until the class interface has been fully resolved, as they may need to access other class members. So, a per-function approach is unlikely to work.\n\nAnother option I didn't mention earlier is to store the necessary context in `pending_body_resolution_lambdas` or `LambdaNode`, and then restore (and subsequently reset back) it in `resolve_pending_lambda_bodies()` (which is already happening with `current_lambda` and `static_context`). This would potentially allow `resolve_pending_lambda_bodies()` to be called at a later time. However, this is not very reliable and only increases the fragility of the current system.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6096655376/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6096682421","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123766#issuecomment-6096682421","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123766","id":6096682421,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABa2P9tQ","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-10T10:44:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T10:44:16Z","body":"I didn't mean to only deffer till the function interface is resolved. I meant pushing into a per-function queue in `resolve_function_signature` and resolving from that queue in `resolve_function_body`. That still ensures the class interface is solved, no?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6096682421/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6097094485","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123766#issuecomment-6097094485","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123766","id":6097094485,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABa2pHVQ","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-10T11:37:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T11:44:54Z","body":"Yes, that could work (though abstract methods need to be checked, since they don't have bodies). But I don't think a separate list/queue _per function_ is necessary; a single common list _per class_ (processed at the end of interface/body class resolution) would suffice (functioning much like the current approach, but without printing an error). Your approach is viable, though slightly more complex: it requires a separate storage, and `reduce_lambda()` needs to be context-aware, i.e. determining whether the lambda is inside a class interface or not, to decide which storage to push the lambda into.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6097094485/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6097359100","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123766#issuecomment-6097359100","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123766","id":6097359100,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABa25Q_A","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-10T12:12:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T12:12:40Z","body":">  a single common list per class (processed at the end of interface/body class resolution) would suffice\n\nAssuming that `current_function` is irrelevant, probably yes. The reason why I suggested per-function, is that it should be possible to completely remove the queue from that approach, by just substituting it with visiting the AST. I figure that might be the best way to prevent any context issues in the future.\n\n> though abstract methods need to be checked, since they don't have bodies\n\n`resolve_function_body` runs on abstract functions. But certainly something to keep in mind, given that it returns very early in that case.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6097359100/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]